  "notes": [
    "GPIO34, 35, 36 and 39 are input only. No output driver and no internal pull-up or pull-down, so every button on them needs an external resistor.",
    "ADC2 (GPIO 0, 2, 4, 12, 13, 14, 15, 25, 26, 27) is taken over by the radio. Anything you read while WiFi is connected has to be on ADC1: GPIO 32 to 39.",
    "GPIO12 must be LOW at boot. It selects the flash voltage, and a pull-up there stops the board starting at all. It is the worst pin on the module to hang a device on.",
    "Other strapping pins: GPIO0 low enters flash mode (the BOOT button), GPIO2 must be low or floating, GPIO5 and GPIO15 are pulled high at boot and emit a PWM burst as they do.",
    "GPIO6 to GPIO11 wire to the SPI flash inside the module. They are not on the 30-pin header, and the 38-pin version that does expose them should not be used.",
    "Any output-capable pin can do PWM: the LEDC block has 16 channels and routes to any GPIO, so the usual PWM pin lists do not apply.",
    "VIN takes 5 V. The onboard regulator handles about 600 mA, and the radio pulls 250 mA spikes, so a thin USB cable shows up as random reboots."
  ],
